{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-9\nattempt=1\nbase=071ff20f9a9e760d635d24bdd7873160a3471345\ncandidate=d088d3ef8892588e7089c8b4d20b600d4624cb7a\n\nDESIGN:\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work without a separate message transport. It does not build group DMs, DM UI, or message posting.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Route | Top-level `POST /api/dms` (task-mandated), not nested under `/api/workspaces/{slug}` |\n| Request body | `{ \"user_id\", \"workspace_id\" }` — both required UUID strings. Task text abbreviated `{user_id}`; **workspace is mandatory** because every channel row has non-null `workspace_id` (MARATHON-5) and the shell lists DMs per current workspace |\n| Response | Always **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }` (not `201`, not a full `ChannelObj` wrapper) |\n| Pair identity | Canonical unordered pair: `user_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])` within a workspace |\n| Dedup without competing for migration v4 | **No new table.** Deterministic synthetic `channels.name` under existing `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)`: `dm-` + first 29 hex chars of `SHA-256(workspace_id \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_lo \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_hi)` (ASCII, lower hex). Satisfies `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`). Lookup = `SELECT` by `(workspace_id, name, is_dm=1)` |\n| Flags | Insert with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, `topic=\"\"`, `is_archived=0` |\n| Membership | On create: insert **both** users into `channel_members`. On get (existing row): **ensure** both memberships exist (re-add if a party previously `leave`d) |\n| Package | New `server/dms/` router + thin store orchestration; channel row helpers live in `server/channels/store.py` next to `create_channel` |\n| DM privacy vs workspace owner | **Tighten** read/mutate gates for `is_dm`: channel **membership required**; workspace `owner_id` alone must **not** bypass (diverges from private-channel owner bypass in MARATHON-7 — justified so DMs are not readable by the workspace owner) |\n| List visibility | Keep/adjust `list_channels_for_workspace_user` so DMs never appear to non-members (defense in depth even if `is_private` were wrong) |\n| Migration | **None** for the happy path (avoids collision with MARATHON-8 and MARATHON-12, both designed as **v4**). Optional later `dm_pairs` table is out of scope |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` unchanged |\n| Ids / time | UUID4 channel ids; `utc_now_z()` timestamps |\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|-------------|------------------|\n| Body only `{user_id}` with implicit workspace | Multi-workspace users make the pair ambiguous; channels are workspace-scoped |\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/dms` | Contradicts task path `POST /api/dms` already reserved by MARATHON-7 out-of-scope |\n| New `dm_pairs` table (migration) | Cleaner join, but **v4 is double-booked** by M8/M12; name-hash uniqueness reuses existing UNIQUE and ships without schema races |\n| Username-based channel `name` for display | Usernames allow `_` and up to 32 chars; fail `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` / length; display is asymmetric per viewer anyway |\n| Return full `{channel: ChannelObj}` | Task mandates `{channel_id}`; client refreshes workspace detail for list rows |\n| Global (non-workspace) DMs | No place in current schema; SPA DMs are per-workspace sidebar |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nOpaque synthetic `ChannelObj.name` for DMs (not a human display label). **MARATHON-17** must render DM sidebar labels from the peer `UserObj` (e.g. via `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` or members already known client-side), not from `name`. Until then, `dms-list` may show the synthetic name — acceptable for this backen\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=d088d3ef8892588e7089c8b4d20b600d4624cb7a APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=d088d3ef8892588e7089c8b4d20b600d4624cb7a CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"7da4c8ff-577e-46ec-abb7-b625449ee8f8"}
